# Rust
/target/
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/vendor/*
!/vendor/big-rust-components/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# makepkg work dirs
/pkgbuild/pkg/
/pkgbuild/src/
/pkgbuild/*.pkg.tar.*
/pkgbuild/*.log

# Compiled translations (built during makepkg from po/*.po).
# `po/` is the only translation source of truth. A compiled dev tree
# (locale/<lang>/LC_MESSAGES/<textdomain>.mo) is generated, not committed
# — i18n.rs's dev_locale_dir() probes it as an installed-catalog fallback.
build-locale/
/locale/
*.mo

# IDE / editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# OS / shell scratch
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.envrc.local

# Coverage / instrumentation
*.profraw
tarpaulin-report.html
cobertura.xml

# Python bytecode, wherever the interpreter drops it — `.github/ci` grows a
# cache the moment its unittest suite runs, which is every gate.
**/__pycache__/

# The front-end's PEP 517 output. `package()` builds the wheel itself and
# deletes these first, so a committed copy is never the one that ships — it is
# only a second, stale answer to "what does this package contain".
/app/build/
/app/dist/
/app/*.egg-info/

# Calibration system: virtualenv + ad-hoc artefacts. Models and
# datasets fetched by setup.sh live in $XDG_CACHE_HOME, never inside
# the repo, but cover stray local copies just in case.
scripts/calibrate/.venv/
scripts/calibrate/reports/
scripts/calibrate/signals/
scripts/calibrate/models/
scripts/calibrate/datasets/
# The bench crate's own build output, next to its sources rather than in the
# workspace target/ the rules above already cover.
scripts/calibrate/ladspa_bench/target/

# cargo-mutants run artifacts
/mutants.out*/

# Working notes and benchmark dumps kept beside the repo rather than in it.
# They are investigation records, not project documentation: README.md
# and ARCHITECTURE.md are, and stay tracked.
/ANALISE-*.md
/PLANO-*.md
/DENOISE-*.md
/DPDFNET-*.md
/BIGLINUX-*.md
/denoise-benchmark.json
